  "english": "23. Sunday. Tone 3 [ԲՁ - Second Side]. Fifth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle [Հարց] Tone 6 [ԳԿ]: \"Pre-eternal\" (Նախայաւիտեան). Resurrection Evening Hymn [Համբարձի] Tone 3 [ԲՁ]: \"That Voice\" (Զայն ձայն) and \"Today They Rejoiced\" (Այսօր զուարճացան).\n24. Monday. Tone 4 [ԲԿ - Second Side]. David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n29. Saturday. Tone 1 [ԱՁ - First Side]. Sons of Thunder. Carnival [Eve] of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Sunday. Tone 2 [ԱԿ - First Side]. Sixth [Sunday]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Resurrection Evening Hymn [Համբարձի] Tone 2 [ԱԿ]: \"Wondrous Resurrection\" (Հրաշալի զյարութիւն).\n31. Monday. Tone 3 [ԲՁ - Second Side]. Fast. Canticle [Հարց] Tone 8 [ԴԿ]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of our fathers.\" And see the others according to the order.\nJanuary\n5. Saturday. Tone 8 [ԴԿ - Second Side]. Eve [Jragaluyts] of the Nativity of Christ.\nRoman Septenary 7.\nJanuary\n6. FRIDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The dispensation of eating [non-fasting period] is seventeen days.\n14. Saturday. John the Forerunner.\n15. Sunday. First [Sunday after Epiphany]. Canticle [Հարց] Tone 7 [ԴՁ]: \"Arising of the Only-begotten.\"\n16. Monday. Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.\n17. Tuesday. Anton [Anthony], Triphon, Parsamas [Barsauma], and Onuphrius the Anchorites.\n19. Thursday. Theodosius the King, and the Children of Ephesus.\n21. Saturday. Athanasius and Cyril the Patriarchs.\n22. Sunday. Carnival [Eve] of the Fast of Catechumens [Arachavorats]. And see the others in the First Volume until Transfiguration [Vartavar], keeping the order of this place.\nFebruary\n12. Sunday. Tone 8 [ԴԿ - Second Side]. Great Carnival [Bun Barekendan].\n14. Tuesday. Tone 2 [ԱԿ - First Side]. Presentation of the Lord [Tearndaraj].\nApril\n2. Sunday. Tone 1 [ԱՁ - First Side]. Easter: Day of the Resurrection of Christ.\n7. Friday. Tone 6 [ԳԿ - Second Side]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\nMay\n21. Sunday. Tone 2 [ԱԿ - First Side]. Pentecost (Coming of the Holy Spirit). Carnival [Eve] of the Elijah Fast.\n28. Sunday. Tone 1 [ԱՁ - First Side]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of Resurrection. Canticle [Հարց] Tone 1 [ԱՁ]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe.\"\nJuly\n9. Sunday. Tone 3 [ԲՁ - Second Side]. Transfiguration [Vartavar]. The dispensation of eating [non-fasting period] is four weeks. Look in the First Volume until the Friday of the third week; and on Saturday come here and begin the feasts set down below, which are after the Eight Days [Octave] of the Nativity.\n29. Saturday. Tone 7 [ԴՁ - Second Side]. Gregory the Theologian.\n30. Sunday. Tone 8 [ԴԿ - Second Side]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Հարց] Tone 4 [ԲԿ]: \"Who the heavenly hosts.\" Resurrection Evening Hymn [Համբարձի] Tone 6 [ԳԿ]: \"When they came\" and \"The angel descended.\"\n31. Monday. Tone 1 [ԱՁ - First Side]. Cyriacus and Julietta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Canticle [Հարց] Tone 5 [ԳՁ]: \"Holy art thou, Lord of hosts.\"\nAugust\n1. Tuesday. Tone 2 [ԱԿ - First Side]. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenia the Virgin, and others. Canticle [Հարց] Tone 8 [ԴԿ]: \"To thee, O God.\"",
